1
00:00:00,087 --> 00:00:03,000
In 1998, Brin and Page ranked the

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,400
web with one imaginary surfer

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,200
who clicks links forever.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,175
Where does that surfer

5
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,075
spend its time?

6
00:00:09,667 --> 00:00:12,080
Take four pages and five links.

7
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:13,942
C has three links coming in.

8
00:00:13,942 --> 00:00:15,142
A has only one.

9
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:17,020
On each page,

10
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,095
the surfer clicks one of

11
00:00:18,095 --> 00:00:19,383
its links at random.

12
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:21,058
But fifteen percent of the time,

13
00:00:21,058 --> 00:00:22,283
they get bored and jump

14
00:00:22,283 --> 00:00:23,458
to any page at all.

15
00:00:24,054 --> 00:00:25,179
Now swap the one

16
00:00:25,179 --> 00:00:26,630
surfer for a crowd,

17
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:28,367
with a quarter of it on each page.

18
00:00:28,954 --> 00:00:29,742
Each tick,

19
00:00:29,742 --> 00:00:31,179
eighty-five percent of every

20
00:00:31,179 --> 00:00:32,942
crowd follows the links,

21
00:00:32,942 --> 00:00:34,555
split evenly.

22
00:00:34,555 --> 00:00:36,380
The other fifteen percent scatter

23
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:38,079
over all four pages.

24
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:39,717
After one tick,

25
00:00:39,717 --> 00:00:41,517
C holds fifty-seven percent:

26
00:00:41,929 --> 00:00:43,267
half of A's crowd,

27
00:00:43,267 --> 00:00:45,392
plus everyone from B and D.

28
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:46,992
Keep ticking.

29
00:00:46,992 --> 00:00:49,679
The shares swing, then settle:

30
00:00:49,679 --> 00:00:51,755
A thirty-seven, B twenty,

31
00:00:51,755 --> 00:00:54,279
C thirty-nine, D four percent.

32
00:00:54,279 --> 00:00:55,730
Those shares are PageRank.

33
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:57,171
Look at A.

34
00:00:57,171 --> 00:00:58,633
It has one link in,

35
00:00:58,983 --> 00:01:00,470
yet almost ties C,

36
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:02,220
because that link comes from C,

37
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:03,996
the busiest page,

38
00:01:03,996 --> 00:01:05,445
and C sends A everyone.

39
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:08,696
D has no links in, so it only ever

40
00:01:08,696 --> 00:01:09,995
gets the random jumpers.

41
00:01:10,587 --> 00:01:12,337
So a link is a vote,

42
00:01:12,337 --> 00:01:13,938
worth the voter's own rank,

43
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:15,812
split among all its links.
